    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35973" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phēgeus</span></b> , i, m.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φηγεύς</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the father of Alphesibœa</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab. 244</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phēgēïus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Phegeus</i>, <i>Phegean</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phegeius ensis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					9, 412</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phēgis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φηγίς</span>, <i>daughter of
				Phegeus</i>, <i>Alphesibœa; acc.</i>
			Phegida, <i><span class="en">Ov. R. Am. 455</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
